# Summon: Titan ({3}{G}{G}, 7/7 Enchantment Creature - Saga Giant, reach, trample): "I - Mill five cards. II - Return all land
# cards from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped. III - Until end of turn, another target creature you control gains trample
# and gets +X/+X, where X is the number of lands you control." Bot1 casts it on turn 1 off Black Lotus (green x3), Mox Emerald and
# Mox Ruby; chapter I mills a Forest, a Forest, a Lightning Bolt, a Mountain and a Plains (the graveyard: those five and the
# sacrificed Lotus). On turn 3 chapter II returns the four land cards tapped and leaves the Bolt (the graveyard: Bolt and Lotus).
# Bot2's Island (turn 2) is not a land Bot1 controls. After the Forest Bot1 plays on turn 3 it controls five lands. On turn 5
# chapter III: the Titan itself ("another") and Bot2's Ornithopter ("you control") are refused - Bot1's Ornithopter and
# Llanowar Elves are the choices, and the Elves (1/1) end 6/6 with trample (X = 5); the Ornithopter stays 0/2. On
# turn 6 it has ended, and the Saga, with three lore counters, is sacrificed.

